class Solution {
    public int minimumPushes(String word) {
        int ans = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < word.length(); i++) {
            ans += (i / 8) + 1;
        }

        return ans;
    }
}

Why does (i / 8) + 1 work?
i         	i/8	                   Pushes
0–7        	0	                        1
8–15	      1	                        2
16–23     	2                       	3
24–25	      3	                        4

So every block of 8 characters gets one extra required push.
